<<<P5
fill=S: When agent.source_listing_version_id is set, load the immutable listing
version server-side (SELECT system_prompt/soul/instructions/tools/skills/model/
permission_mode/runtime_kind/sandbox_backend FROM marketplace_listing_versions
WHERE id=$1) and build agentContext/agentContextFromRow from THAT, not from the
renter's workspace_agents row (which is empty). MUST route execution by the
version's runtime_kind: 'builtin' -> runAnthropicCompletion server-side (owner pays
inference / Q2 margin); 'sandbox' -> platform sandbox backend (P8/P9), NEVER the
renter daemon; force-skip the hasMcpPresence and run_mode==='daemon' branches for
installs. MUST NOT persist the system-prompt-composed text into agent_jobs.prompt
(keep prompt='' like the builtin branch; agent_jobs is renter-db-selectable). MUST
NOT copy owner secrets: install turns read ONLY the renter workspace's own secrets,
never the owner's (F7). Emit a usage_ledger row per turn per the listing price_model
(P2): meter='task'/'request' -> qty 1; meter='seconds' -> finished_at-started_at.
>>>
PLAN P6<-F7 op=insert at=server/index.cjs:2334#"  if (runMode === 'builtin') {" why=phase2-secret-boundary ref=database/neon-schema.sql:47-56#"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS workspace_secrets (",server/index.cjs:785 test="MANUAL QA: set an owner-workspace secret, run rented instance in renter workspace, assert the secret value never appears in the renter runtime env or job payload" order=2 fill=S
<<<P6
fill=S: Enforce the secret boundary as an explicit policy gate. Owner secrets
(workspace_secrets of the listing's owner_workspace_id) are NEVER injected into any
install turn: builtin server-side turns inject only the renter workspace's secrets;
sandbox turns get owner secrets ONLY if the platform runs the sandbox (server->E2B
direct env, never server->renter-daemon). Add a guard helper resolveTurnSecrets(agent)
that returns renter secrets for installs and refuses to read owner_workspace_id
secrets unless runtime_kind==='sandbox' AND the backend is platform-hosted. Day-1
(Q3) accept builtin-only (no code-exec, no owner secrets) for prompt-only listings.
>>>
