PLAN P9<-F3 op=insert at=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:409#"function buildAgentCommand(config, job) {" why=phase3-sandbox-backend-abstraction ref=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:413-452,agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:237-240 test="cd agent/agensis-cli && node --check src/agensis.mjs" order=3 fill=-
<<<P9
// F3: pluggable execution isolation. A SandboxBackend wraps how the built command
// is actually run. Selected by the job's runtime descriptor (job.sandbox_backend,
// defaulting to config). Contract:
//   interface SandboxBackend {
//     id: 'process' | 'local_sb' | 'e2b';
//     // prepare a jailed workdir + env allowlist; returns an execution handle.
//     prepare(job, { cwd, envAllowlist }): Promise<SandboxHandle>;
//     // spawn the coding CLI inside the jail; must stream stdout/stderr like the
//     // current child_process path so createStreamJsonParser still works.
//     spawn(handle, cmd, args, { onStdout, onStderr }): Promise<{ exitCode:number }>;
//     cleanup(handle): Promise<void>;
//   }
// Implementations:
//   ProcessBackend  (id 'process')  — today's direct child_process.spawn in host cwd;
//                                     the default for OWNER-run agents only.
//   LocalSandboxBackend (id 'local_sb') — macOS `sandbox-exec` (sb-style) profile OR a
//                                     restricted temp cwd + scrubbed env; no network by
//                                     default; for renter-side installs the owner allows.
//   E2BSandboxBackend (id 'e2b')     — E2B cloud sandbox via @e2b/code-interpreter;
//                                     server injects owner secrets directly (never the
//                                     renter host). Platform-hosted tier for paid listings.
// selectSandboxBackend(config, job) => picks by job.runtime_kind/sandbox_backend.
// fill=S: author the three classes + selector; route resolveJobExecution through
// selectSandboxBackend(...).prepare/spawn/cleanup instead of the inline spawn.
>>>
PLAN P10<-F6 op=insert at=server/index.cjs:5393#"  // --- Connect an MCP client (one workspace token)" why=phase3-install-and-publish-routes ref=server/index.cjs:4028-4055#"  const columns = [",server/index.cjs:2288#"async function runAgentTurn" test="MANUAL QA: publish agent from workspace A, install into workspace B, confirm a workspace_agents instance row appears in B with empty system_prompt and source_listing_version_id set" order=3 fill=S
<<<P10
fill=S: Authenticated routes. (a) POST /backend/workspaces/:id/agents/:agentId/publish
-> snapshots the current workspace_agents config into a new marketplace_listing_versions
row (F11 immutable), upserts marketplace_listings (slug/title/media/pricing/runtime),
sets current_version_id. Requires 'manage'. (b) POST /backend/marketplace/listings/:slug/install
-> creates agent_installs (pins current_version_id) + a THIN workspace_agents row in the
caller's workspace: name/avatar/handle/description copied, but system_prompt/soul/
instructions EMPTY, source_listing_id/source_listing_version_id/install_id set,
runtime_kind from the version. Requires 'manage' on the renter workspace; grants NO
membership in the owner workspace (F6/F9). Existing dispatch/@mention/claim_job then
work unchanged because the instance is an ordinary local row. (c) For paid listings,
create the Stripe Connect subscription/checkout before activating the install.
>>>
